From: local private research
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi_osal: Use start_creating_path()/end_creating_path()

6.18 replaced the kern_path_create()/done_path_create() pair with
start_creating_path()/end_creating_path() and dropped the old names from
include/linux/namei.h, so mt_diag_create_directory() no longer sees any
declaration of them:

  mt_osal_diag.c:594:10: error: implicit declaration of function
  'kern_path_create' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

The new functions are exported and keep the same contract: the returned
dentry holds the parent lock and a write reference on the mount, which
end_creating_path() releases. Keep the old names for older kernels.

Signed-off-by: local private research
---
--- a/mt_osal_diag.c
+++ b/mt_osal_diag.c
@@ -591,7 +591,11 @@
 	struct path path;
 	int err;
 
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+	dentry = start_creating_path(AT_FDCWD, name, &path, LOOKUP_DIRECTORY);
+#else
 	dentry = kern_path_create(AT_FDCWD, name, &path, LOOKUP_DIRECTORY);
+#endif
 	if (IS_ERR(dentry)) {
 		MT_DEBUG_TRACE("Error create!\n");
 		return PTR_ERR(dentry);
@@ -606,7 +610,11 @@
 #endif
 	if (!err)
 		MT_DEBUG_TRACE("create %s OK!\n", name);
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+	end_creating_path(&path, dentry);
+#else
 	done_path_create(&path, dentry);
+#endif
 	return err;
 }
 
